# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# MicrobeGraph — what the container build must NOT receive
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS:
#   When you run a build, the engine first sends this whole folder to
#   the build process. Without filtering, that means .venv/ (hundreds of
#   MB), data/ (potentially gigabytes), and .git/ — all copied for nothing.
#
#   It is also a SECURITY file. A secret that reaches an image is baked
#   into a layer, and deleting it in a later layer does NOT remove it.
#   Anything inside a published image is effectively public.
#
# Read by BOTH Docker and Podman.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------

# Rebuilt inside the container from requirements.txt — and it would be the
# WRONG platform's binaries anyway (macOS packages inside a Linux image).
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Secrets — must NEVER be baked into an image.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.streamlit/secrets.toml
*.pem
*.key

# Rebuilt by the pipeline; often gigabytes.
data/
*.duckdb
*.duckdb.wal
*.db
*.sqlite

# Version history — not needed at runtime, often the largest folder.
.git/
.github/

# Python working files
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Not needed to RUN the app (docs are for humans reading the repo).
docs/
notebooks/
figures/
tests/

# R working files — the library is huge and rebuildable from renv.lock.
renv/library/
renv/staging/
.RData
.Rhistory
.Rproj.user/

# Private scratch space — never enters an image either.
.dev/

# Editor and operating-system clutter
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
